3. Findings
====================================================================

N1 (must fix, B6.1). The recorded `sympy_verification.call` strings do not
reproduce the recorded result. 110 of 422 recorded simplify() calls give a
different answer when re-run as written (20 integral, 90 identity). Example,
substitution-001:
    call   simplify(diff(x**2 - 2*x, x) - 2*x - 2)     recorded result 0
    run as written: 2*x - 2 - 2*x - 2 = -4
The generator computes the right thing (generate_corpus.py:191, :201, :239,
:244 subtract SymPy objects). Only the text is wrong: the f-strings at
generate_corpus.py:211-213, :228-229, :254 and :268 drop the parentheses
around the subtracted operand. Correct rows also write `"result": "0"` as a
literal (:231, :269, :376) after an assertion, instead of the printed residual.
This is AGENTS.md rule 3 and rule 4 in spirit: an evidence string that gives
a different answer when someone runs it. Fix: parenthesise the operand, write
sympy.sstr(residual) for every row, regenerate, and show that the diff
touches only `call` and `result` fields.

N2 (goes into V8). The 4 ln rows are marked `expressible: false`, and
tests/corpus.rs prints "SymPy-disproved claims cannot be expressed as a B5
rejection". That label is wrong. The claims parse, and verify_identity runs
on them. They are not outside the language. B5 returns a false Verified on
them. The freebuff message and b6-evidence.log lines 390-400 do say this in
plain words, so nothing was hidden. Only the flag name misleads. V8 removes
the flag and makes the domain arm 17/17.

N3 (note). CI captures test stdout, so the "13/13" and "4" lines appear only
in freebuff's local --nocapture transcript (b6-evidence.log), not in the CI
log. CI shows only:
  test domain_claims_are_rejected_where_the_claim_language_can_express_them ... ok
  test sympy_ground_truth_corpus_is_accepted_and_mutants_rejected ... ok
  test result: ok. 2 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.07s
The assert_eq!(rejected, 13) in the test still pins the count, so CI does
enforce it.

N4 (rule 4). freebuff's message calls mathd/target/wasi-runner.mjs "the
committed WASI runner". It is not tracked:
  $ git ls-files mathd/target/wasi-runner.mjs | wc -l
  0
Fix in B6.1: commit it at a tracked path (target/ is ignored), or correct the
text. Every local wasm32 result in b6-evidence.log depends on it.

====================================================================
4. B5 reopened: V8 (domain mismatch gives a false Verified)
====================================================================

freebuff's evidence (b6-evidence.log lines 390-393):
  domain-014 ln(x^2) = 2*ln(x)        Verified (16 points, 1.1e-16)     NOT REJECTED
  domain-015 ln(x^3) = 3*ln(x)        Verified                         NOT REJECTED
  domain-016 ln(sqrt(x^2)) = ln(x)    Verified                         NOT REJECTED
  domain-017 ln(x^4) = 4*ln(x)        Verified                         NOT REJECTED

The lead confirmed the cause in the code:
  $ grep -nE "is_finite|continue;|Err\(_\)" mathd/src/verifier.rs
  261:                // If either value is non-finite, skip point (outside domain)
  262:                if !g.is_finite() || !e.is_finite() {
  263:                    continue;
  285:            (Err(_), _) | (_, Err(_)) => {
  286:                // Point is outside the common domain of the expressions; skip it.
  287:                continue;
A point where one side is defined and the other is not is skipped as if
neither side were defined. ln(x^2) is defined for x < 0 and 2*ln(x) is not,
so every negative point is thrown away. The claim is then "confirmed" on
positive points alone. The equation path has the same pattern (lines 400,
423, 447). This is a false Verified, the failure the B5 work order calls
project-stopping. B5 is unticked in plan.md.

A missing root is a different question (V4, membership versus the full
solution set). It stays with the owner.

