====================================================================
WHAT I COULD NOT DO
====================================================================
- I did not run cargo test natively. This host has no linker. The plant ran
  through freebuff's untracked WASI runner (N4). If that runner is wrong, the
  local results are wrong too. CI on Linux is the independent run.
- I did not check whether the 8 error kinds are realistic student mistakes.
  The names match the spec. Realism is a judgment call, not a test.
- I did not test the V8 fix shape. A strict rule (one side defined, the other
  not, means Failed) may reject some SymPy-true corpus rows, for example
  integrals whose antiderivative has a smaller domain than the integrand.
  The corpus will show this when V8 is built.

====================================================================
WHAT I AM UNSURE OF
====================================================================
- Whether the owner wants identities judged on the common domain or with
  matching domains. The lead's default for V8 is strict: domains must match
  at every sampled point. Strict can only reject more. It is logged in
  decisions.md as overridable.
- My first oracle pass had 38 false alarms (plain simplify). The stronger
  pass cleared all 38. If the stronger pass is also weak, it errs toward
  rejecting correct rows, not toward accepting wrong ones.

VERDICT: PASS (B6 content verified independently, 551/551 true and 746/746 false; B6.1 required for N1 call strings and N4 runner; B5 reopened as V8)
